  "rationale": "No facts yet, so I seed the two throughput-friendly families. The 50 MSPS constraint forces 1 result/cycle, so only pipelined/pipelined_m qualify. I focus on the accuracy-feasible corner: W=14-18 and N=12-18 with round rounding and small guards keep max_abs_err <= 2^-12 while leaving room for the Fmax>=50 MHz constraint. pipelined_m is the likely power winner because it trades a few registers for a shorter critical path, so I give it a meaningful share to map the power-vs-accuracy trade-off; pipelined anchors the high-accuracy end of the front."
